== Trivia ==
=== Etymology ===
* Aleph is the first letter of the Semitic abjads.
* Aleph numbers are a sequence of numbers used in mathematics, particularly set theory, to represent the size of infinite sets. Aleph-1 is the second smallest of these numbers, with the smallest being Aleph-0.